  "task": {
    "id": "roman-to-numeral",
    "title": "roman-to-numeral",
    "statement": "The roman package exposes is_roman_numeral (already implemented) and a stub to_roman(n). Implement to_roman(n) so that it converts an integer n in the range 1..3999 inclusive to its standard Roman numeral string using subtractive notation (4='IV', 9='IX', 40='XL', 90='XC', 400='CD', 900='CM'). Return a str. Raise ValueError when n is an int outside 1..3999. Raise TypeError when n is not an int (bool counts as non-int for this task is not required; treat only real ints as valid). Do not change is_roman_numeral or the tests.",
